1. The driver currently can be built as a built-in driver only.
   Built as a kernel module(.ko) is failed on pass of options

2. the default bootup resolution is 640x480-8bpp

3. driver options can be passed by appending boot option:

   video=rdcfb:opt1,opt2,...
   
   options:
       mode=[xres]x[yres]-[bpp]
       
   Example 1 for 800x480 as bootup resolution, use default color depth:
       kernel  /boot/vmlinuz-2.6.28-16-generic root=UUID=6fea54d8-67ee-4dec-8367-d6bc4d93b74f ro noreplace-paravirt quiet splash video=rdcfb:mode=800x480
   
   Example 2 for 800x480-16bpp as bootup resolution:
       append video=rdcfb:mode=800x480-16

4. menuconfig:
   built-in "Framebuffer Console support"
   add and set built-in "CONFIG_FB_RDC" in %source%/drivers/video/Kconfig

5. put driver directory in %source%/drivers/video/rdc

6. Add "obj-$(CONFIG_FB_RDC) += rdc/" into %source%/drivers/video/Makefiel

